Rostro is licensed under multiple licenses, applied per-crate and per-file.

Default for new Rostro Foundation contributions and for the on-chain runtime
(all sp-* primitives, all frame-* and pallet-* runtime crates):

    Apache License, Version 2.0    -- see LICENSE-APACHE

Default for the substrate-client (sc-*) crates retained from upstream Parity:

    GNU General Public License, Version 3 or later,
    WITH Classpath-exception-2.0   -- see LICENSE-GPL3-CLASSPATH

The split is documented in NOTICE.md, including the runtime/node boundary,
the rationale for the Classpath exception, and the practical implications
for downstream consumers and patent holders.

Per-file SPDX-License-Identifier headers in source files are authoritative.
Where a file's SPDX tag disagrees with the per-crate Cargo.toml license
field or this top-level LICENSE pointer, the per-file SPDX tag wins.
